      "description": "China calls Pakistan its \"iron brother\", but does that friendship end where unpaid bills begin? In this episode, we examine explosive claims made by prominent Pakistani journalist Aftab Iqbal that Beijing is delaying J-10CE fighter jet spare parts and holding back the J-35A stealth fighter because of Pakistan's mounting CPEC debt. While neither China nor Pakistan has officially confirmed these allegations, the claims have reignited questions over Islamabad's growing dependence on Chinese military hardware and financing. We also analyse Pakistan's worsening debt crisis, the unresolved financial disputes surrounding CPEC, China's leverage over Pakistan's defence ecosystem and what this means for the Pakistan Air Force. Could unpaid infrastructure loans now affect military cooperation? Is Pakistan's dependence on Chinese weapons becoming a strategic vulnerability? Watch this detailed analysis as we separate verified facts from unverified claims and examine the bigger geopolitical picture.",
